{"title":"Compliance Officer Roadmap","role":"Compliance Officer","summary":"A Compliance Officer helps an organization identify, understand, implement, monitor, and report compliance with applicable laws, regulations, internal policies, contractual obligations, and industry standards.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Business Law (BBA LLB / B.Com LLB)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Compliance Officer helps an organization identify, understand, implement, monitor, and report compliance with applicable laws, regulations, internal policies, contractual obligations, and industry standards."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BBA LLB/B.Com LLB graduate, this is a strong career path because it combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law","Business","Finance","Risk","Governance","Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Compliance Officers can work in banks, fintech companies, financial institutions, technology companies, pharmaceutical companies, manufacturing organizations, listed companies, consulting firms, law firms, insurance companies, and multinational corporations."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Compliance Officer” is a broad corporate role rather than one single regulated professional title. Certain sectors and specific statutory compliance positions can have additional qualification, experience, certification, or registration requirements. For example, company-secretarial responsibilities may require the applicable professional qualification where the law requires it."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Typical Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Corporate Compliance"},{"text":"Monitoring compliance with corporate laws and policies"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Compliance"},{"text":"Tracking sector-specific regulations"